WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.375
So what does the code add?

2
00:00:01.375 --> 00:00:05.838
Four commands and an entry script,
added to the module from Chapter 1.

3
00:00:05.838 --> 00:00:08.226
One checks the accounts
against the standard.

4
00:00:08.226 --> 00:00:11.287
One writes the alert query
from the account IDs.

5
00:00:11.287 --> 00:00:15.387
One wraps that query in a deployable
template, without deploying it.

6
00:00:15.387 --> 00:00:20.900
And one runs the same match over exported
rows, so you can review a drill offline.

7
00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:24.869
Two small files drive it: one
names the accounts and their

8
00:00:24.869 --> 00:00:28.838
exclusion group by object ID,
and one records every drill.

9
00:00:28.838 --> 00:00:32.660
It reuses Chapter 1's reader,
so it only ever reads.
